# Tiny commits

When committing this repo, make **the smallest commits that still make sense**.

- One idea per commit. Do not bundle unrelated files.
- Prefer one file per commit when the changes are independent (README vs CSS vs gameplay).
- If a feature needs several files, split by layer: model, then AI, then UI copy.
- Commit message says why, in one sentence. No laundry lists.
- Never squash a pile of work into one "misc updates" commit.
- Do not wait until the end of a task to commit a dump; commit as each slice lands.

Examples:

- `Add a snub-nose .22 revolver that rolls 2–15 damage.`
- `Show geezers as purple dots on the minimap.`

Not:

- `Update game, docs, and URLs.`
